================================================================
FINAL TEAM MERGE AND INTEGRATION SEQUENCE
================================================================

1. Vighnesh completes and merges Prompt 1.1.
2. Everyone pulls the stable main branch.
3. Santosh starts Prompt 3.1.
4. Rohan starts Prompt 4.4.
5. Vighnesh completes Prompt 1.2, then 1.3, then 1.4, then 1.5.
6. Vighnesh merges each Batch 1 prompt individually.
7. Everyone pulls after each Batch 1 merge that changes shared fields.
8. Vighnesh starts and merges Batch 2 prompts in order.
9. Santosh merges 3.1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4, and 3.5 in order.
10. Rohan merges 4.4, 4.2, 4.3, 4.1, and 4.5 in order.
11. Vighnesh performs final integration testing.
12. Team fixes integration bugs before final delivery.


Rules that prevent duplicate or conflicting work:

- Do not run a shared-file prompt on multiple PCs at the same time.
- Do not merge a pull request with unresolved conflicts.
- Do not change API fields after another team member starts using them.
- Pull before starting each prompt.
- Push or submit only after local testing.
- Merge one prompt at a time.
- Announce every merge to the team.
- Keep database, backend, and frontend field names identical.
- Keep demo behavior compatible with live API behavior.
- Ask Vighnesh before changing any core shared file.
